## The split this vault exists to enforce

A private bank cannot let an advisory tool blur what happened with what might
happen. So the two are not merely labelled differently here — they live in
different folders, and the builder refuses to put one in the other.

### `Verified/` — the record

Settled fact. Every note is derived from rows in `data/` and nothing else. No
figure in a headline was written by a language model; each one was computed and
is listed under **Computed values**, with the exact rows it came from under
**Sources**. Follow the links and you end at the dataset.

**This is the folder an RM can put in front of a compliance reviewer.** A claim
in here that cannot be traced to a row is not a presentation problem, it is a
bug — and one the build refuses to produce.

### `Scenario/` — the hypothesis

Forward-looking analysis: what a portfolio would look like under conditions that
have not occurred. Useful, and not the same kind of thing as the folder above.
Nothing here is a statement about what happened, and nothing here may be shown
as one.

See [[About Scenario]]. *Currently empty by design — no scenario analysis has
been generated yet.*

### `Sources/` — the raw rows

One note per dataset row that any fact cites, reproduced as it appears in
`data/`. This is the end of the chain: there is nothing behind these notes.

